---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Our First Press Trip: L.A. Comic Con — T-Time Media"
  description="Five halls, hundreds of booths, and a lot more trans representation than I expected. T-Time Media's first press trip, to L.A. Comic Con."
  ogPath="/press/comic-con"
>
  <Header />

  <!-- ================= ARTICLE ================= -->
  <section id="about">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Press · L.A. Comic Con · Los Angeles</h2>
      <p class="page-title">Our first press trip: L.A. Comic Con</p>
      <p class="lede">Five halls, hundreds of booths, and a lot more trans representation than I expected.</p>
      <p class="fineprint" style="margin:20px 0 36px;">By Dominic Anthony Pérignon · T-Time Media</p>
      <div class="doc">
        <p>T-Time Media is an independent media company run by trans folks, and we did something we'd never done before: we went to Comic Con in LA as press.</p>
        <p>I applied for press access, and we got in. I'm Dominic, the founder of T-Time Media, and I'll be honest, I had no idea what I was walking into.</p>

        <h3>Bigger than I thought</h3>
        <p>I thought I knew how big it would be. I was wrong. There were five halls, and every one of them was packed with booths. Hundreds of them. Comics, characters, celebrities, and more. You could spend the whole day in one hall and still feel like you missed half of it.</p>

        <h3>Every corner felt different</h3>
        <p>What stuck with me most is how different every corner felt. The event has whole sections for Artist Alley, autographs, and photo ops. One minute you're looking at hand-painted miniatures and signed comic art. The next you're staring at a custom gaming PC with an octopus glowing inside it. In South Hall there were immersive experiences, and the Día de los Muertos display, with candles, marigolds, and skulls, was one of the most beautiful things I saw.</p>
        <p>There was a main stage with surprise performances, and you never knew what was coming next. And the cosplay was incredible: a Jack Skellington, a character with a TV for a head, and plenty more.</p>

        <h3>Seeing trans stories in the comics</h3>
        <p>I was surprised to see trans representation at Comic Con. I spoke to someone who created a comic of about 25 stories, including some about transgender characters. I grabbed a sticker, listened to a few things he had to say, and moved on to see what else was around.</p>

        <div class="figure">
          <span class="big">Throughout the entire event, I noticed no fear and no judgment, just a whole lot of comics.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= WHY THIS MATTERS ================= -->
  <section id="why" style="background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);border:0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 style="color:var(--accent);">Why we do press work</h2>
      <div class="two-col">
        <div>
          <p class="lede" style="color:#fbfaf7;">T-Time Media is run entirely by transgender people. That's why we do press work in the first place.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>Trans people are usually the topic of someone else's story. We'd rather be the ones telling it. A press badge puts us in the room, with the camera, deciding what gets covered and how.</p>
          <p>It also lets us show trans folks that they belong in places like Comic Con. And we get to cover trans people the way we actually live: finding comics with characters like us, geeking out over cosplay, and just enjoying the day. Not as a debate. As people.</p>
          <p>We're independent, so no outlet tells us which stories count. That means we can spend time on creators who don't get much attention, like the creator I met who made a comic of about 25 stories, some of them with trans characters. Press coverage helps small creators get seen, and we want to be part of that.</p>
          <p>And yes, there's a practical side too. Press access opens doors to events, interviews, and partnerships, and that helps us keep doing this work.</p>
          <p>Walking the halls, I felt no fear and no judgment, just a whole lot of comics. We want to make more of that visible.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= FROM THE FLOOR ================= -->
  <section id="floor">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>From the floor</h2>
      <div class="work">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="seg">Photo to add</span>
          <p class="t">DSC08301</p>
          <p class="d">The welcome sign at the L.A. Comic Con entrance.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="seg">Photo to add</span>
          <p class="t">DSC08323</p>
          <p class="d">Collectible figures lined up on a booth shelf.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="seg">Photo to add</span>
          <p class="t">DSC08344</p>
          <p class="d">A custom gaming PC with an octopus glowing inside.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="seg">Photo to add</span>
          <p class="t">DSC08360</p>
          <p class="d">The Día de los Muertos display, with candles, skulls, and marigolds.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="seg">Photo to add</span>
          <p class="t">DSC08336</p>
          <p class="d">A Jack Skellington cosplay in the hall.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="seg">Photo to add</span>
          <p class="t">DSC08373</p>
          <p class="d">The T-Time crew at work with press badges on.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="fineprint" style="margin-top:28px;">Comic Con recap video — coming soon. Footage by Carter Nelson.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= WHAT'S NEXT ================= -->
  <section id="next">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What's next</h2>
      <p class="lede">This was our first press trip, and it won't be our last.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/opportunities">See what's open →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
